@startuml bootwire_transaction_flow
!include ../_style.iuml
title <size:21><color:#1B3A5F><b>One Transaction</b></color></size>\n<size:13><color:#5B6B7C>one request in flight; a resend uses the same SEQ and is answered from the cache</color></size>

box "Host (PC)" #F4F7FB
  participant "<b>Host</b>\n<size:11><color:#C9D7E6>BootWireClient</color></size>" as H #1B3A5F
end box
box "Target (Cortex-M bootloader)" #EEF6F4
  participant "<b>Target</b>\n<size:11><color:#CBE6DF>bootloader</color></size>" as T #146C5F
end box

H -> T : Request  [SEQ=n, CMD, PAYLOAD, CRC16]
activate T
note right of T
  check CRC, look up reply cache,
  execute, cache the reply
end note
T --> H : Response [SEQ=n, CMD|0x80, STATUS, PAYLOAD, CRC16]
deactivate T
note over H, T
  Exactly one request is in flight. The next request uses SEQ = n+1.
  No valid response in time: the host resends the **same** frame (same SEQ).
  The target answers a resend from its cache, so a command never runs twice.
end note
@enduml
